## Why This Question Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design a privacy-conscious OTCA telemetry path with idempotent ingestion, multi-tenant governance, and basic QoS guarantees. It also assesses practical considerations for browser-based collaborative applications.

## Key Concepts Covered
- OTCA telemetry modeling with event_id for deduplication
- Exactly-once ingestion semantics at the edge gateway and Kafka
- PII redaction at ingestion with per-tenant residency enforcement
- Client-side sampling to bound data volume

## Reference Implementation
```javascript
// Ingest endpoint with idempotency and PII redaction
async function ingestEvent(rawEvent) {
  // 1. PII redaction: Hash user_id before storage
  const sanitizedEvent = {
    ...rawEvent,
    user_id_hash: hashUserId(rawEvent.user_id),
    user_id: undefined // Remove raw PII
  };

  // 2. Idempotency check for edit_apply events
  if (rawEvent.event_type === 'edit_apply') {
    const exists = await checkEventIdExists(rawEvent.event_id);
    if (exists) return { status: 'duplicate', event_id: rawEvent.event_id };
  }

  // 3. Route to tenant-specific Kafka partition
  await kafka.produce({
    topic: `tenant-${rawEvent.tenant_id}`,
    messages: [{ value: JSON.stringify(sanitizedEvent) }]
  });

  return { status: 'accepted', event_id: rawEvent.event_id };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes governance architecture across OTCA, focusing on immutability, auditability, regional residency, and rollback semantics in policy updates.

## Key Concepts
- Region residency and local sinks
- Versioned, immutable policy logs
- Global reconciler with audit trail
- Rollback and cross-region consistency

## Code Example
```javascript
function isNewVersion(current, incoming) {
  const toNum = s => (s||'0').split('.').map(n => parseInt(n,10));
  const [a,b,c] = toNum(current);
  const [x,y,z] = toNum(incoming);
  if (x !== a) return x > a;
  if (y !== b) return y > b;
  return (z||0) > (c||0);
}
```

